      "side": 1,
      "message": "(connected to this line, but it\u0027s more of a general issue I think - but I can\u0027t find a way to leave a general comment that is not connected to anything)\n\nI ran this suite locally against a 3-node cluster twice. It failed both times, at two different steps.\n(Fresh cluster staging, no leftover state from the previous run)\n\n\tRun 1\n - step_create_device_data: 500 from the POST to node 2. From member-2\u0027s\nkaraf.log, the netconf topology singleton was still re-electing when the write\narrived:\n```\n  13:45:14,926  SlaveSalFacade         | Slave mount point registered.\n  13:45:16,509  SlaveSalFacade         | Slave mount point unregistered.\n  13:45:16,965  NetconfTopologyContext | Leader was selected: 127.0.1.0\n  13:45:17,131  NetconfTopologyContext | Follower was selected: 127.0.1.0\n  13:45:17,131  NetconfTopologyContext | Instance is already closed.  (WARN)\n```\nThe POST landed in the ~600ms window after the slave mount was unregistered.\nstep_wait_for_device_data_to_be_seen does not protect against this: it waits for a successful *read* through node 2, which is satisfied at 14,926 while the slave mount is briefly registered, and the state then regresses.\n\n\tRun 2\n - got past that step, ran all 16384 edits, and failed at\nstep_check_for_failed_requests with 20 x \"Status code: 500\". Those map 1:1 onto\nmember-1 (the device master) logging:\n```\n  Can not perform commit when lock is released on device\n  RemoteDeviceId[name\u003d17830-sim-device, address\u003d/127.0.1.0:17830]\n```\n20 errors, 20 failed requests, matching withing few ms, spread across ~73s\nof the run rather than clustered at the start.\n\nAs far as I can tell, both fails seem to come down to writes being routed through a non-owner node reaching the device master while its lock/mount state is still unstable.\n\nI hit exactly this while porting the Entity and Outages suites. At the end I handeled it there with an ownership-settled gate before write (plus a retry that reads the value back).\nhttps://git.opendaylight.org/gerrit/c/netconf/+/124551\n\nThat approach doesn\u0027t map onto this suite cleanly though, so I am not 100% sure what to do.\n\nWhat do you think the best approach here is?",
